 "text": "Hello there, how are you? Stick to the sidewalk or wide walkway where you can see and be seen from behind a bench or car. Don't try turn between them. Sorry for any frustration they face. Offer a little wave and a smile as you pass, and keep moving quickly. Much better than stopping traffic. Stop, get off, and then let the car go first. It' only one or two minutes, and it's the safest approach. I know it is. Lots of adults still get scared, even after riding it for years. Just take deep breaths and remember the safest is always after.",
